    "prompt": "If $2x+2y=14$ and $x^2-y^2=21$ then $x-y$ is equal to",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "1"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "2"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "3"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "4"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$-1$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Difference of squares",
        "body": "From $2x+2y=14$ we get $x+y=7$. Then $x^2-y^2=(x+y)(x-y)=7(x-y)=21$, so $x-y=3$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 3**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Solve for x and y",
        "body": "$x+y=7$ and $x^2-y^2=21$ give $x-y=3$ by division; check: $x=5,y=2$, $25-4=21$ and $x-y=3$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 3**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "algebra"
    ],
