    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Algebra",
        "body": "Let the integers be $n-1,n,n+1$. Then $(n-1)^2+n^2+(n+1)^2=3n^2+2=770$, so $n^2=256$, $n=16$ and the largest is $17$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 17**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Estimate",
        "body": "The squares average $770/3\\approx257$, so the middle number is close to $16$. Check: $15^2+16^2+17^2=225+256+289=770$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 17**"
      }
