      }
    ],
    "answer": "E",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Reflect the vertex",
        "body": "If the $x$-axis is an axis of symmetry, the reflection $(-1;1)$ of the vertex $P=(-1;-1)$ is also a vertex. $P$ and $Q=(-1;1)$ are then either adjacent vertices (side $2$; the square lies to the left or to the right of $PQ$: $2$ squares) or opposite vertices (diagonal $PQ$: $1$ square). That is $3$ squares. Similarly the $y$-axis gives $3$ squares. The square with vertices $(\\pm1;\\pm1)$ is symmetric about both axes, so it was counted twice: $3+3-1=5$.\n\n**Answer: (E) 5**"
      }
    ],
