        "title": "Equilateral triangle",
        "body": "$FECG$ is a kite with $EC=CG$ (the sides meeting at $C$). $G$ is the centre of the rhombus, so $CG=\\frac12CA$, and $EC=\\frac12BC$. Then $CA=BC$. Since $BC=AB$ (rhombus), triangle $ABC$ is equilateral. $AE$ is a median, so it is also the bisector of $\\angle BAC=60^\\circ$, giving $x=30^\\circ$.\n\n**Answer: (C) $30^\\circ$**"
